{"id": "EUVD-2026-77010", "enisaUuid": "66a511e9-e53b-3052-ad8a-043be2d302d4", "description": "MKVToolNix through 101.0 contains a heap buffer overflow in the bundled avilib library's ODML superindex parser due to integer wraparound in 32-bit arithmetic. Attackers can craft a malicious AVI file with oversized entry counts that cause an undersized heap allocation, allowing a heap buffer overflow when the file is parsed with mkvmerge.", "datePublished": "2026-09-13T12:22:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-30T19:07:45", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://codeberg.org/mbunkus/mkvtoolnix/commit/1495126138e086080f0163bee27fafbdf956a1d0", "https://codeberg.org/mbunkus/mkvtoolnix/src/tag/release-101.0/lib/avilib-0.6.10/avilib.c#L2552-L2570", "https://codeberg.org/mbunkus/mkvtoolnix", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/mkvtoolnix-through-101.0-heap-buffer-overflow-via-avilib-odml-superindex-integer-wraparound"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x9xf-h66v-mjmc", "CVE-2026-90783"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b9478ba1-bb9b-3724-970d-2cdd623808e3", "product": {"name": "MKVToolNix", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u2264101.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a121c320-fd08-3374-b6c8-d9233a43e67f", "vendor": {"name": "Moritz Bunkus"}}], "isExploited": false}